[Music]  the playstation 4 pro represents a new  move for Sony while the company has  refreshed many of its consoles before  the ps4 Pro marks the first time a mid  generational design has received a  significant boost in processing power is  it worth it let's find out one of the  first things you'll notice about the ps4  pro is that it's 11.6 by 2.1 by 12 inch  chassis is big at 7.2 pounds it's also  quite heavy in terms of aesthetics it  maintains the ps4 s a slanted design but  ops to use the ps4 Slim's more rounded  corners as opposed to the originals  sharper edges the console has a new  power LED light bar on the front which  starts on the left and trails off to the  right coupled with the light bar or  physical power and eject buttons the pro  sort of looks like a ps4 slim stacked on  top of the original ps4 and as two slits  that go around the chassis  despite being a 4k capable system the  pro doesn't support 4k blu-ray discs  this is an odd and unfortunate omission  which slightly detracts from the package  in terms of ports the pro brings back  the optical spit off' which was removed  from the ps4 slim in addition to the two  USB 3.1 ports on the front the pro  offers a third USB 3.1 port on the back  like the original ps4 and ps4 slim  before it the pro model has an  integrated power supply which saves you  the trouble of figuring out where to  position a bulky external power brick  inside the chassis the faster graphics  processing unit is arguably the most  significant boost the ps4 pro offers the  GPU is based on AIM these new Polaris  micro architecture which the graphics  card manufacturer debuted with its  Radeon R X 480 GPU it's 911 megahertz  frequency is 14% higher than the  original models equivalent  it also offers twice the number of  compute units with 36c use and features  4.2 teraflops of performance which is to  point to a times as much as the original  ps4 the console itself still offers  eight gigabytes of gddr5 memory which it  shares with the CPU but sony has added  one gigabyte of traditional dram of the  CP  this allows the x86-based processor to  run the operating system and streaming  video applications at 4k this extra dram  also frees up some of the faster gddr5  memory for the GPU the CPU is still an 8  core Jaguar AMD processor but its  frequency has been raised from 1.6  gigahertz to 2.1 gigahertz which amounts  to a 31% boost the ps4 pro also comes  with a larger 1 terabyte hard drive the  main reason to get excited about the ps4  pro is the prospect of better graphics  the new console is completely backwards  compatible with the existing ps4 library  and some games will receive graphical  enhancements on the pro some titles may  use the extra processing power to  bolster frame rates while others may  render at a higher resolution some games  may run natively at 4k but sony says the  majority of games will use a 4k  upscaling technique a company called a  checkerboard rendering which is  essentially a 4k rendering shortcut that  isn't as taxing on hardware it's not  quite as sharp as native 4k but it does  look surprisingly close ps4 games will  not receive Pro enhancements out of the  box however developers will have to  patch their games to take advantage of  the pros extra processing power  developers can actually use the added  power as they see fit instead of  cranking up the resolution developers  may choose to increase graphical  fidelity or offer improved frame rates  or use better anti-aliasing this means  the pro could bolster visuals at 1080p  to analyze the visual enhancements that  the ps4 Pro offers I compared it against  a regular ps4 I hooked up both  Playstations to different HDMI inputs on  the same TV a 55 inch 4k HDR display I  gather two copies of every ps4 Pro  enhanced games that I could get copies  of and quickly switched between the two  inputs to conduct visual a be tests  because the ps4 Pro can also bolster  1080p graphics I also connected both  systems to a 55 inch 1080p TV and  similarly analyze the visual differences  there for my full analysis I suggest you  read my in-depth written review but the  big takeaway here is that the ps4 Pro  offers a better anti-aliasing that  mitigates unwanted jaggies this is  especially true on the 4k TV this makes  the overall image look sharper and  cleaner for instance in the remastered  version of modern warfare it's easier to  make out the individual hair follicles  on an NP  is beer these aren't mind-blowing  editions by any means but they are  appreciated anti-aliasing effects do  carryover ever-so-slightly at 1080p -  but they're much less noticeable  speaking of 1080p shadow of mordor  offers a super sampling anti-aliasing  with the pro which can make a regular  old HD display look a little sharper  than it actually is some HDR enabled  games like The Last of Us an infamous  second son provide more vibrant and  realistic colors looking up at the sky  in the pro version of second son  I noticed pink streets of light fill out  the clouds this effect wasn't as  prominent on the slim where everything  looked a little more video gaming black  levels also look really black in the  game - a little too black in fact with  textures getting smothered in ultra dark  shadows the PlayStation 4 pro can indeed  make games look better that is if their  patch to take advantage of the extra  processing power but should you buy a  ps4 Pro if you have a 4k HDR TV and are  looking to buy a console I definitely  recommend the pro even if you have a  1080p TV and are looking to buy a  Playstation  I'd still lean towards Sony's newest  console yes it does cost hundred dollars  more than the slim model but you get  more ports twice the storage more  future-proof hardware and some games can  look slightly better at 1080p if you  already have a ps4 however I wouldn't  make the upgrade unless you have a 4k  HDR TV and the extra cash lying around  graphics enthusiasts may appreciate the  improved anti-aliasing and more vibrant  colors but the difference is likely  won't blow you away regardless the ps4  Pro is priced fairly offers a plethora  of features and as the most powerful  console you can buy today for more on  the ps4 Pro check out GameSpot calm &amp;  subscribe to our youtube channel  by  [Music]

